  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-14",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-14",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "sb fitness ct700 self generated curved treadmill",
      "sb fitness ct700",
      "ct700 curved treadmill",
      "sb fitness ct700 vs ct550",
      "sb fitness curved treadmill",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See Who It Suits", link: "#who-it-suits" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-sbfitnessct700curvedtreadmill" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-sbfitnessct700curvedtreadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          SB Fitness CT700 <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Self-Generated Curved Treadmill</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The CT700 is the flagship of SB Fitness Equipment’s own curved treadmill range: a self-powered machine with eight magnetic resistance levels, stainless steel track bearings and a 19-inch deck, sold mostly direct for about $2,600. It is a credible sprint and sled-push machine on paper, provided you read its figures as the seller’s and get the weight rating and warranty confirmed in writing.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#listed-specifications" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            The Listed Specifications
          </a>
          <a href="#ct700-vs-ct550" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            CT700 vs CT550
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/" rel="author noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Author and lab tester</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.4k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What is claimed, what conflicts, and what we have not done.</strong>
          On 14 October 2026 we read the CT700 listing, its scratch-and-dent listing, the CT700 owner's
          manual and setup tips sheet, and the shipping and return policies on SB Fitness Equipment's own
          store, together with the seller's CT700 comparison article, and compared them with an
          independent walking-equipment catalogue that records the listing and manual, and with retailer
          and review listings. The seller's product page and the independent catalogue agree on the
          figures used on this page — the 19 x 66.6 in. running surface, eight magnetic resistance
          levels, stainless steel track bearings, 308 lb machine weight, 13.5 in. step-up height and the
          warranty shown on the product page. The maximum user weight conflicts across the seller's own
          documents (400 lb on the product page, 475 lb in the manual, 350 lb in its comparison article),
          and the manual gives a different running surface, length and warranty; we state each as a
          conflict. We found no independent measurement or long-term review. We have not tested the CT700.
          Prices change; confirm the price, specification and warranty before you order.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. The SB Fitness CT700 Self-Generated Curved Treadmill: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#who-sells-it" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. What the CT700 Is, and Where It Is Sold</a>
          <a href="#listed-specifications" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The Listed Specifications, and Where They Conflict</a>
          <a href="#ct700-vs-ct550" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. SB Fitness CT700 vs CT550: What the Extra $600 Buys</a>
          <a href="#how-it-works" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. How the CT700 Works, and What It Is Like to Use</a>
          <a href="#warranty-and-returns" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Warranty, Returns, Delivery and Assembly</a>
          <a href="#who-it-suits" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. Who It Suits, and What to Consider Instead</a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. The Verdict</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The SB Fitness CT700 self-generated curved treadmill is real, in stock in limited numbers, and
          sold mainly through one place: SB Fitness Equipment's own online store. Almost everything known
          about it comes from that seller — its product page, its owner's manual and its own comparison
          articles — and those sources do not always agree with each other, most importantly on the
          maximum user weight. This page sets out what is listed, where the seller's documents conflict,
          how the CT700 differs from the cheaper CT550 we reviewed alongside it, and who it suits.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. The SB Fitness CT700 Self-Generated Curved Treadmill: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The SB Fitness CT700 self-generated curved treadmill is a real, currently sold curved
            treadmill with eight magnetic resistance levels, stainless steel bearings and a long 19-inch
            deck, priced at $2,595 direct, and almost everything known about it comes from the company that
            sells it.</strong> On its listing it is a strong value for sprinting, intervals and sled-push work:
            it does much of what $3,500 to $5,500 curved treadmills do for considerably less.
          </p>
          <p>
            The caveats are specific. The seller's own documents give three different maximum user weights —
            400 lb on the product page, 475 lb in the owner's manual and 350 lb in its comparison with the
            AssaultRunner — and the manual's warranty pages disagree with the product page and with each
            other. We found no independent measurement of the CT700 and little independent coverage at all.
            Delivery is kerbside for a 308 lb machine, assembly has enough pitfalls that the seller publishes
            a tips sheet for it, and change-of-mind returns carry a 20% restocking fee unless you take store
            credit.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you want a curved treadmill for hard training and do not need app connectivity, the CT700 is
            worth a close look, especially next to the cheaper
            <a href="/sb-fitness-ct550-curved-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">SB Fitness CT550</a>
            from the same seller, which we compare below. Our
            <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best curved treadmills</a>
            roundup covers the better-documented alternatives, and our
            <a href="/curved-treadmill-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">curved treadmill guide</a>
            explains whether a curved machine suits you at all. We have not tested the CT700.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Product cards -->
      <div class="not-prose">
        {
          PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-white font-black text-xl leading-tight m-0">
                      {index + 1}. {product.name}
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 flex-wrap">
                    <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400">Typical street price</span>
                    <span class="ml-auto font-black text-gray-900">{product.priceRange}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-4">{product.specs}</p>
                  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6" set:html={product.description} />
                  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-green-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.pros.map((pro) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{pro}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-red-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Don't Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.cons.map((con) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{con}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
                    <p class="text-gray-900 font-bold mb-4">{product.bottomLine}</p>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
                      <a href={product.amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
                        {product.amazonLabel} &rarr;
                      </a>
                      {product.reviewUrl && (
                        <a href={product.reviewUrl} class="text-[#0F62FE] font-bold no-underline text-sm hover:underline">
                          Read our full {product.name} review &rarr;
                        </a>
                      )}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="who-sells-it" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. What the CT700 Is, and Where It Is Sold</h2>
<p>
            SB Fitness Equipment is a small US fitness retailer that sells Body-Solid, Vision and Spirit
            equipment alongside its own SB Fitness range of curved treadmills: the CT250 walking model, the
            CT400, the CT550, the CT700 and the cherry-wood CT850 SprintMaxx, currently on pre-order. The
            CT700 is the seller's "flagship performance curved treadmill", aimed at serious athletes, personal
            trainers, HIIT, sled-push training and small commercial or studio use. It has been on the
            seller's store since late 2022.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Price and stock</h3>
          <p>
            On 14 October 2026 the seller listed the CT700 at $2,595 against a $3,695 "compare at" price,
            with a note that inventory was very limited and the next shipment was expected by 1 November. A
            scratch-and-dent CT700 — a unit returned within the 30-day window, which may have cosmetic marks
            — was listed at $2,245 and described as in stock and shipping within one to two business days.
            Treat the compare-at price as a reference rather than a measure of value; the direct price is what
            the machine sells for.
          </p>
          <p>
            Outside the seller's own store, the picture is thin. A Walmart category page showed the CT700 at
            $2,895, which we could not confirm as a current listing, and we found no Amazon listing; the
            independent catalogue we checked also describes it as sold only through the brand. Buy it from SB
            Fitness Equipment or from a major marketplace listing that names SB Fitness as the seller, and be
            wary of unfamiliar web stores, which on the sister CT550 have carried contradictory figures.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="listed-specifications" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. The Listed Specifications, and Where They Conflict</h2>
<p>
            The seller's product page and the independent catalogue that records it agree on most figures.
            The seller's owner's manual and its own comparison article disagree on several. The table shows
            each figure and its status.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Item</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Product page</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Other seller documents</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Running surface</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">19 x 66.6 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Manual: 66 x 19 in</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">400 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Manual: 475 lb; comparison article: 350 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Machine weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">308 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Manual and article agree</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Assembled size</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">78 x 34 x 62 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Manual: 76 x 34 x 62 in</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Step-up height</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">13.5 in</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not in manual</td></tr>
