        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying an SB Fitness CT700</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most of the risk with the CT700 sits in its paperwork, its size and its terms rather than in the hardware. These are the four mistakes to avoid.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Relying on one weight rating</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The seller lists 400 lb, its manual 475 lb and its comparison article 350 lb. If you are near the top of that range, or buying for a studio, get the rating for your unit confirmed in writing before you pay.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for steel bearings you will not use</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The CT700’s main advantage over the CT550 is sustained high-speed sprinting. If you mainly run at moderate pace or do HIIT, the CT550 is $600 cheaper, 127 lb lighter and lower to step onto.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Starting assembly without the tips sheet</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Assembly is where CT700 complaints cluster. Connect the console cable before bolting the left handlebar, start every bolt by hand before tightening, and check the hardware bag before assuming cover screws are missing. Have a second person for the handrails.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not pricing in the restocking fee</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 20% restocking fee on a $2,595 machine is about $520, plus packing a 308 lb treadmill to freight standard. Clearance items cannot be returned at all. Try a curved treadmill first if you can, and decide whether you would accept store credit.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
